text I descend the slope alone.
text Until a few weeks ago, the trees were full of peach-colored petals.
text I look up to find a green tunnel that's terrible on the eyes.
text Beyond that is the unchanging blue sky of late afternoon.
text @[Tomoya]
text (I didn't have anything...)
text A realization comes to me suddenly.
text I didn't have anything to motivate me and I couldn't find anything new...
text After my father became like that, I didn't want to go anywhere near my house...
text Everything just seemed like a huge pain in the ass...
text "I'm the only one who's special. The rest of the world is boring."
text I felt as if taking that attitude absolved me.
text But now...
text Now I have a goal.
text I want to hear Kotomi play her violin.
text @[Tomoya]
text That's not a bad goal...
text I whisper that out loud to nobody in particular.
